Author:     ivanfioravanti <ivan.fioravanti@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Oct 20 07:43:32 2026 +0200
Commit:     ivanfioravanti <ivan.fioravanti@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 08:09:09 2026 +0200

    Read narrow decode copies of the V4.1 router and Engram projection
    
    The GGUF widens two decode weights: the BF16-source router is stored as
    F32 and the Engram projection, an E4M3 checkpoint, as F16. Decode now
    reads a BF16 copy of the router and the exact E4M3 codes with their
    32x32 block scales, built once at graph allocation and freed with the
    engine. The E4M3 matvec maps each code to an F16 bit pattern (exactly
    value / 256, subnormals included) instead of decoding it.
    
    Logits are bit-identical. Decode at 2K on M3 Ultra: 38.5 -> 39.2 t/s;
    the Engram projection drops from 849 to 658 us per token.
    
    DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_ROUTER_BF16=1 and DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_ENGRAM_E4M3=1
    restore the wide reads.

